    slug: `an-interview-with-vladimir-petrov-the-runner-up-of-the-nashville-international-chopin-piano-competition-on-a-shigeru-kawai`,
    title: `An Interview with Vladimir Petrov: The Runner Up of the Nashville International Chopin Piano Competition on a Shigeru Kawai`,
    datePosted: `January 14, 2026`,
    content: `Vladimir Petrov on Winning the Nashville International Chopin Piano Competition and the Shigeru Kawai SK-EX Nashville International Chopin Piano Competition finalist Vladimir Petrov shares his journey to success and his experience performing on the world-renowned Shigeru Kawai SK-EX concert grand piano.

A Moment of Triumph at the Nashville Chopin Competition For pianist Vladimir Petrov, being selected as a finalist and receiving an award at the Nashville International Chopin Piano Competition represents the culmination of intensive preparation and dedication. "I feel incredibly happy and honored to receive this award," Petrov reflects. "After a long period of preparation, it is a great relief, and I am very much looking forward to future engagements representing the competition."

The Perfect Partnership: Vladimir Petrov and the Shigeru Kawai SK-EX When asked about his experience performing on the Shigeru Kawai SK-EX, Petrov's response reveals the immediate connection with the instrument. "From the very first touch, I knew it was the right choice for my program," he explains. "Everything felt easy and effortless, with a full, warm timbre that allowed me to shape the sound naturally." Music as a Living Laboratory For Petrov, music represents more than performance—it's "my passion and my profession, a musical laboratory where I can discover something new every day, something to feel and something to reflect upon." Through his performances, Petrov aims to share his deep admiration for the music itself: "its narrative, its emotional depth, and its sense of surprise." This philosophy of continuous discovery drives his artistic vision. Looking Forward As Petrov looks to the future, his aspirations remain rooted in musical exploration and connection. He plans to "continue enjoying the experience of sharing meaningful music with ever wider audiences, and to keep discovering new facets of my musical journey." About the Nashville International Chopin Piano Competition: A premier platform for emerging pianists specializing in the works of Frédéric Chopin, this competition showcases exceptional talent on world-class instruments including the Shigeru Kawai SK-EX concert grand. About Shigeru Kawai: Handcrafted by master artisans in Japan, the Shigeru Kawai SK-EX represents the pinnacle of piano craftsmanship, chosen by competition winners and concert artists worldwide for its exceptional tonal warmth and responsive touch. Visit Shigeru Kawai`,
